# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code — per-machine local settings
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.claude/settings.local.json` is Claude Code's per-developer override file
# (a machine-specific Bash/tool permission allowlist that embeds absolute
# home paths). The shared `.claude/settings.json` IS committed; the `.local`
# variant must stay local so one developer's paths + grants never leak into
# the shared repo. The generic `*.local` rule above does NOT match a
# `.local.json` suffix, so this explicit entry is required.
#
# DELIBERATE EXCEPTION (owner decision, 2026-07-26): the ROOT
# `.claude/settings.local.json` IS tracked. The owner wants their accumulated
# permission allowlist to travel with the repo across machines and sessions
# rather than be rebuilt each time. The negation below keeps that one file
# tracked while `**/settings.local.json` still protects every other location.
# Consequence to be aware of: it embeds one machine's absolute home paths, so
# treat edits to it as machine-specific and avoid clobbering another dev's
# copy. Review the diff before committing changes to it — same discipline as
# `.claude/sessions/` (see that directory's README).
**/settings.local.json
!.claude/settings.local.json

